text pp0386 "<p class=\"agents-none\">No AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md yet: the shared rules apply, then the README.</p><a class=\"box-link box-link-source source-link\" href=\""
text pp0387 "\">README on GitHub</a>"
text pp0388 "<section class=\"section\" id=\"rules\"><h2>The shared rules</h2><p>These are the working rules of every AIEN agent, published word for word. My own agents also read a few rules that only work on the project's own machine (its local services, hardware reservations and how to report to the operator). Those are left out because an outside agent cannot follow them.</p><ul class=\"card-grid\"><li class=\"hub-card agents-card\"><a href=\"/agents/RULES.md\">RULES.md</a><ol class=\"agents-rule-list\">"
text pp0389 "public/agents/RULES.md"
text pp0390 "</ol><a class=\"box-link box-link-source source-link\" href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/aienos.com/blob/main/public/agents/RULES.md\">Source on GitHub</a></li></ul></section>"
text pp0391 "<article class=\"prose agents-page\"><header class=\"page-intro\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">For agents</p><h1>Point your agent at any AIEN repository</h1><p class=\"lede\">Every public AIEN repository is listed here, including archived repositories for reference. Give your agent two files: the shared rules, and the repository instructions linked below under their actual filename, AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md. Your own subscription pays for the work (Claude, Codex, Gemini, Grok or any other agent).</p></header><section class=\"section\" id=\"start\"><h2>Start an agent</h2><ol><li>Pick an active repository below and open its linked instructions: they say what the repository is, how to build and test it, and what needs approval.</li><li>Paste this into your agent, with the repository's address in place of the example:</li></ol><pre class=\"agents-prompt\">Read https://www.aienos.com/agents/RULES.md and then the repository instructions (AGENTS.md, or CLAUDE.md if that is the file listed) at https://github.com/aien-dev/omega-mv, and follow both. Pick an open issue in an active repository, comment to claim it, work on a branch, and open a pull request that leads with the evidence: the commands you ran and their output. Archived repositories are listed for reference; do not assume they accept contributions.</pre><p>Your agent works through ordinary pull requests. It needs no access to the project's machines, and only reviewed, merged work reaches the record on <a href=\"/now/\">Now</a>.</p></section>"
